#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "CAP-STORAGE Object storage"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Durable object storage for tables and files, isolated per domain catalog."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: data"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Tables and files are stored durably, and each domain's data sits behind its own location and credential."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Giving each domain its own location means a grant on one domain can't reach another domain's files. Source files are the evidence behind every number derived from them, so they're kept as records ([P12]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "An object API, reached by identity."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "One location and one credential for each domain catalog."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "An archive area for source-of-record files."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-storage.md
msgid "Object versioning on a lake store can conflict with table maintenance, because deleted data files come back as old versions and maintenance can't reclaim the space. Use the table format's history and backups for recovery instead, and test the combination."
msgstr ""

